      "math_academy_id": "q-81219",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Let $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where ${b}_{1}=2{c}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2}=-5{c}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{c}_{1}+5{c}_{2} \\\\  & =5{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(2{c}_{2})-\\frac{3}{5}(5{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{b}_{1}+\\frac{3}{5}{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}].$",
